{
 "summary": "This bill proposes several changes to education requirements for participating students and schools. Parents of participating students would be required to ensure their children take all annual Tennessee comprehensive assessment program (TCAP) tests (or state-authorized successor tests) required for their grade or course. Students in grade 11 must take the examination required for public school students in that grade, and students in kindergarten through grade three must annually take three approved universal reading screeners during established windows. Students with disabilities who use alternate assessments as determined by their IEP are exempt. Test results must be reported to the student's parent.

Participating schools would be required to publish their lesson plans, syllabi, academic standards for every class, and a current list of library materials on the school's website. For these purposes, library materials include items like books, films, video games, and subscription content provided to students. Additionally, participating schools must ensure all their educators hold a valid public school teaching license issued by the state board of education. 

The bill would take effect on July 1, 2025."
}
